# RiteMark Patch: exact save receipts
#
# Purpose: Bind Ritemark's local-save receipt to the exact logical text snapshot handed to the file service.
#
# Why: Reading the file path from onDidSave can race with an external writer and suppress a real two-writer conflict.
#      A save VS Code refuses as newer, for a document Ritemark's editor holds, goes to Ritemark's document sync first, so the person
#      gets one question (Ritemark's Review changes) or none (only the file's date or line endings moved), never two (#454).
#      A file that changed under a clean document Ritemark's editor holds goes to Ritemark before VS Code reloads it, so
#      Ritemark merges the writer's copy with the person's text instead of the file's text replacing it (#588).
#
# File(s): src/vs/workbench/api/browser/mainThreadDocuments.ts, src/vs/workbench/api/common/extHost.protocol.ts, src/vs/workbench/api/common/extHostDocumentData.ts, src/vs/workbench/api/common/extHostDocuments.ts, src/vs/workbench/contrib/files/browser/editors/textFileSaveErrorHandler.ts, src/vs/workbench/contrib/files/test/browser/ritemarkSaveConflict.test.ts, src/vs/workbench/services/textfile/common/textFileEditorModel.ts, src/vs/workbench/services/textfile/common/textFileEditorModelManager.ts, src/vs/workbench/services/textfile/common/textfiles.ts, src/vs/workbench/services/textfile/test/browser/textFileEditorModel.test.ts
# Created: 2026-08-31
# Updated: 2026-10-19 (Sprint 135: carried onto VS Code 1.142.0 unchanged)
# Updated: 2026-10-26 (Sprint 137, #454: the save-error handler hands a refused save to Ritemark, with VS Code's notification when no answer comes within 3 s: textFileSaveErrorHandler.ts and its test)
# Updated: 2026-11-01 (Sprint 145, #588: the reload participant: `ritemarkReloadParticipant` on the model manager, asked in `resolveFromFile` before a clean model takes a changed file's text, the file's text made only when Ritemark's editor holds the model; an undo of Ritemark's answer never makes the model clean; the save-error handler's contribution answers with `_ritemark.editorSync.answerReload` within 3 s, else VS Code reloads as before)
#
